B.3.2 Crib, playpen toys and mobiles 
See 4.11.5. 
Mobiles intended to be mounted on a crib, playpen, wall or ceiling should be provided with instructions for 
proper assembly, installation and use to ensure that the product does not present an entanglement hazard. 
The instructions should include at least the following information: 
⎯ a crib mobile is not intended to be grasped by a child; 
⎯ if attached to the crib or playpen, remove when a baby begins to push up on hands and knees; 
⎯ if mounted on a wall or ceiling, install the mobile clearly out of a standing baby's reach; 
